`wexample/symfony-content` is a small Symfony bundle for rendering authored content — Markdown files and the code blocks inside them — in an application's Twig templates. It registers a `markdown_file` Twig function that reads a file relative to the kernel's project directory ({{ path("src/Twig/MarkdownExtension.php") }}), and ships a front asset, {{ path("assets/ts/code-block.ts") }}, that highlights `.code-block[data-lang]` elements and Markdown `<pre><code class="language-…">` blocks with Shiki. It targets Symfony 8.2+ projects already built on `wexample/symfony-helpers`, where documentation or editorial pages live as Markdown files in the repository rather than in a database.
